24. Chapter III of the Act
of 1948 deals with health and obliges the

factories premises to be kept clean (
Section 11
), disposal of wastes

and effluents (
Section 12
), ventilation and temperature (
Section 13
),

regulation of dust and fume (
Section 14
), artificial humidification

(
Section 15
), regulations of overcrowding in rooms (
Section 16
),

provision for lighting (
Section 17
), provision for drinking water

(
Section 18
) and provision for latrines and urinals (
Section 19
).
